<title>USA: First Bell sets one-time cash distribution.</title>
<headline>First Bell sets one-time cash distribution.</headline>
<dateline>BELLEVUE, Pa. 1996-12-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>First Bell Bancorp Inc said Tuesday it plans a one-time cash distribution of $3 per share, payable December 31, record December 20.</p>
<p>First Bell said it expects $2.95 per share of the distribution would be treated as a return of capital and would not be subject to income tax until the shares are sold.</p>
<p>First Bell Bancorp, which is the holding company of Bell Federal Savings and Loan Association of Bellevue, operates seven full-service offices in the Pittsburgh metropolitan area.</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk 212-859-1611))</p>
